{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 8, :comments ["<b>First interpretation</b><br>בְּעִקְבֵי הַצֹּאן (in the tracks of the sheep). Like וַעֲקֵבֹתֶיךָ לֹא נוֹדָעוּ (and your tracks were not known)." "גְּדִיּוֹתָיִךְ. A גְּדִי without עִזִּים is any young of clean livestock." "<b>Second interpretation</b><br>He [i.e. the speaker] answers her: if you do not shepherd, go out for yourself in the tracks of the sheep and shepherd the young kids, just as you are younger than the dwellings of my companions — and this is my station." "<b>Third interpretation</b><br>The Shekhinah answers her: if you do not know, go in the way of your fathers, and your children who are born will graze upon the path of the tribes."], :book :song-of-songs, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 1, :notes {0 "Parenthetical gloss appears in the Hebrew source; rendered as part of the comment.", 2 "Bracketed Hebrew letters [לה] and [צאי] in the source appear to indicate variants or insertions; resolved as integral to the quoted phrase.", 3 "Bracketed letter [ה] before שכינה may indicate an inserted definite article; rendered as 'the Shekhinah.'"}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra's commentary on the Canticles" "http://beta.nli.org.il/he/books/NNL_ALEPH002030344/NLI"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:43:50.110064332Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}